## Discipline (doctrine-loop Arm 3 — docs are verified-not-trusted)
- When you read a doc to inform work, sanity-check its load-bearing claims against code/state/git. Stale = a bug you found.
- Stale-on-sight = fix-now (small/safe) or flag with `file:line` (bigger). Never knowingly leave a doc lying to the next agent.
- Behavior change → same-PR doc update. Grep for the docs/comments/briefs describing the changed behavior.
- Adding/retiring/re-authoring a doc → update this index row in the same change.
- This index is the **just-in-time routing layer** of the project's context system: agents load docs THROUGH it when a task needs them. Doc content is never inlined into `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`/rules (the always-on layer stays lean and pointer-based — bootstrap Step 2.5).
